        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "on the X-side, and symmetrically with  $ \\mathbb{E}[t u^2] $ on the Y-side, with  $ \\gamma = 0 $ recovering the covariance decomposition of Cook et al. (2023) exactly and  $ \\gamma = 1 $ the pure coskewness objective. The weight  $ \\gamma $ is a single interpretable knob trading regime sensitivity (large  $ \\gamma $) against predictive sharpness on smooth data (small  $ \\gamma $).",
            "block_bbox": [
                136,
                791,
